    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d352">

                <pb facs="0440" n="1274" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1274"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/407</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-13T19:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 13, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8222. For Sheldon [from
                    War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 652. Referring further Embassy’s 10364, May 31, 3 p.m., your 690.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d352-f1"/> The following note was delivered to the Swedish
                    Minister by the Department on June 10: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Referring to our conversation of Thursday morning and in order that there
                            can be no further misunderstanding on the subject of the shipping
                            agreement, I beg to say that the War Trade Board does not insist on the
                            four months’ charter of the replacing vessel which <pb facs="0441"
                                n="1275" xml:id="pg1275"/> come from Sweden under the <hi
                                rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi>. The Board merely insists
                            that the replacing ships shall leave coincidentally with, or prior to,
                            the departure from the United States for Sweden of the boats operating
                            under the <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi.</hi>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
